* [WARNING] ERROR_HANDLING Missing response validation and error handling (at fetchProfile)
  - Issue: The function assumes the API always returns a JSON object with a profile property containing displayName and avatarUrl. If the response lacks profile (e.g., {error: "not found"}) or profile is null, accessing body.profile.displayName throws a TypeError, crashing the caller. Similarly, non‑2xx HTTP status codes are not checked, so error responses are treated as data.
  - Fix: Validate the response before using it:
    ```js
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`);
    const body = await res.json();
    if (!body?.profile) throw new Error('Invalid profile response');
    const { displayName, avatarUrl } = body.profile;
    return {
      name: (displayName ?? '').trim(),
      avatar: avatarUrl || "/static/default.png",
    };
    ```

* [WARNING] INJECTION Missing URL encoding of path parameter (at fetchProfile)
  - Issue: The id argument is directly interpolated into the URL template `/users/${id}`. If client.get performs naive string concatenation, an id like "../../etc/passwd" could escape the intended path segment, potentially exposing sensitive files or causing unexpected requests.
  - Fix: Ensure the id is safely encoded before interpolation, e.g.:
    ```js
    const encodedId = encodeURIComponent(id);
    const res = await client.get(`/users/${encodedId}`);
    ```
